{{/* filter: the page-wide lens on a sticky ground-coloured dock. The sentinel div
     lets verso.js detect the pinned state (the dock gains .verso-filter-stuck and
     the bar breathes in). The dock bleeds past the content column (-mx-10/px-10, the
     page's own padding) so pinned rows slide fully beneath it, dissolving through
     the ::after gradient fade. Behaviour is shell-owned: see verso.js. */}}
<div class="h-px"></div>
{{/* pt-10 = the content column's own 40px gutter, so the pinned bar sits as far
     from the top as the content does from the sidebar. Constant padding — a
     pin-time change would shift the page, and the lens never moves anything. */}}
{{/* top offset is owned by the stylesheet (components layer), not a utility —
     it must yield to the subpage top bar when one is present. */}}
<div class="verso-filter-dock sticky z-20 -mx-10 bg-ground px-10 pt-10 pb-3">
  {{/* the lens is a field like any other field — the page's own hairline, the
       page's own ground — because what makes it findable is that it is always
       the first thing on the page, not that it is painted louder than the
       listing it sifts. It warms to the action colour under the pointer and
       when it has the caret, the way every control here does. */}}
  <div class="verso-filter-bar flex h-9 items-center gap-2.5 rounded-xs border border-rule-strong bg-ground px-3 transition-colors hover:not-focus-within:border-faint focus-within:border-denim">
    {{icon "search" "size-4 shrink-0 text-faint"}}
    <input type="search" data-verso-filter placeholder="{{.}}" aria-label="{{ t "Filter everything on this page" }}"
      class="w-full border-0 bg-transparent text-sm text-ink outline-none placeholder:font-normal placeholder:text-meta">
    <kbd class="shrink-0 rounded-xs border border-rule-strong px-1.5 font-mono text-xs leading-4 text-meta" aria-hidden="true">/</kbd>
  </div>
</div>
